 parts:\n\n$$\n7\\times 7=49\n$$\n\nFinally, we join the above with the block of zeros: \n\n$$\n490000=490,000\n$$\n\nTherefore, ${700}^{2}=490,000.$" 13194139534642 17592186045417 true] [17592186430709 1068 #edb/ref 17592186430702 13194139534642 17592186045417 true] [17592186430709 1069 "q-224170" 13194139534642 17592186045417 true] [17592186430709 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 13194139534642 17592186045417 true] [17592186430709 1071 "${14}^{2}=${{field-1}}" 13194139534642 17592186045417 true] [17592186430709 1072 #uuid "e43445a0-0d82-5a10-9128-a6bbc70f2fb7" 13194139534642 17592186045417 true] [17592186430709 1074 "To evaluate ${14}^{2},$ we start by writing it out with a multiplication sign:\n\n$$\n{14}^{2}={{14\\times 14}_{⏟}}_{2\\text{ times}}\n$$\n\nThen, we work out $14\\times 14.$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned} & \\begin{aligned} &  &  & \\,\\,\\,\\,\\begin{aligned}\\boxed{} \\\\ \\boxed{1}\\end{aligned}\\,\\,\\,\\, &  \\\\  &  &  & \\,\\,\\,\\,1\\,\\,\\,\\, & \\,\\,\\,\\,4\\,\\,\\,\\, \\\\ \\,\\,\\,\\,\\times \\,\\,\\,\\, & \\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\, & \\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\, & \\,\\,\\,\\,1\\,\\,\\,\\, & \\,\\,\\,\\,4\\,\\,\\,\\, \\\\  &  & \\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\, & \\,\\,\\,\\,5\\,\\,\\,\\, & \\,\\,\\,\\,6\\,\\,\\,\\, \\\\ \\,\\,\\,\\,+\\,\\,\\,\\, & \\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\, & \\,\\,\\,\\,1\\,\\,\\,\\, & \\,\\,\\,\\,4\\,\\,\\,\\, & \\,\\,\\,\\,0\\,\\,\\,\\, \\\\  & \\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\, & \\,\\,\\,\\,1\\,\\,\\,\\, & \\,\\,\\,\\,9\\,\\,\\,\\, & \\,\\,\\,\\,6\\,\\,\\,\\,\\end{aligned} & \\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, ${14}^{2}=196.$" 13194139534642 17592186045417 true] [17592186430710 1068 #edb/ref 17592186430703 13194139534642 17592186045417 true] [17592186430710 1069 "q-224334" 13194139534642 17592186045417 true] [17592186430710 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045486 13194139534642 17592186045417 true] [17592186430710 1071 "Given that ${26}^{2}=676,$ evaluate ${26}^{4}.$" 13194139534642 17592186045417 true] [17592186430710 1072 #uuid "f2152ba3-455d-5581-bc1a-a5346e3a47